   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Magnetic Cursor\n\nA page drawn through a WebGL shader that warps every pixel toward a moving cursor, with a Gaussian falloff and a little chromatic aberration, plus a repel pulse. Four captions explain what is happening.\n\nCategory: shaders. Length: 15 s. WebGL: yes.\n\nUse when:\n- A demo of an interactive-looking page where pixels bend toward a cursor, for tech and product videos.\n- A text-and-cards screen that should feel alive without changing its layout.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The shot is just a backdrop with no content: the shader only bends the built-in page.\n- You need the effect on your own video footage: copy the shader into your composition and feed it your frame as a texture.\n\nVariables:\n- heading (string): Heading, default \"Pixels bend toward your [cursor]\"\n- body1 (string): Paragraph 1, default \"Move your mouse across this page. Every pixel is drawn through a WebGL shader that warps space toward your cursor position, like a magnet pulling iron filings beneath a thin rubber sheet.\"\n- body2 (string): Paragraph 2, default \"The distortion follows a Gaussian falloff: strong at close range, tapering smoothly to nothing. The text remains readable even under deformation.\"\n- hint (string): Hint line, default \"WebGL2 shader distortion over a live page\"\n- cards (string): Cards, default \"Real-time | 60fps distortion over the whole page in one shader pass; Crisp type | The page is drawn at full fidelity before it is bent; GPU shaders | Gaussian warp plus chromatic aberration in one fragment shader\"\n- captions (string): Captions, default \"The whole page is drawn through a WebGL shader; A magnetic shader warps every pixel toward the cursor; Chromatic aberration splits RGB channels at the distortion site; A repel pulse pushes the page away again\"\n- background (color): Page background, default \"#0c0c0c\"\n- ink (color): Heading colour, default \"#f0f0f0\"\n- accent (color): Accent, default \"#70c7ed\"\n- strength (number, 0-3): Pull strength, default 1\n- resolution (number, 0.25-1): Resolution, default 0.75\n\nSource: heygen-com/hyperframes. Licence: Apache-2.0. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
